{"name":"Crushed Ice","hex":"#c4fff7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of crush"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pulverized, rendered into small, disconnected fragments.","Broken, saddened, depressed, devastated."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crushed"},{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice cube","blocks":[{"text":"An ice cube is a small piece of ice, which is typically rectangular as viewed from above and trapezoidal as viewed from the side. Ice cubes are products of mechanical refrigeration and are usually produced to cool beverages. They may be made at home in a freezer with an ice tray or in an automated ice-making accessory. They may also be produced industrially and sold commercially."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ice_cubes_openphoto.jpg/330px-Ice_cubes_openphoto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_cube","wikidata":"Q488463"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Gorrie_Ice_Machine.png/330px-Gorrie_Ice_Machine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Gorrie_Ice_Machine.png/330px-Gorrie_Ice_Machine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gorrie's ice machine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGorrie_Ice_Machine.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Hielos.jpg/500px-Hielos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Hielos.jpg/1280px-Hielos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Hielos.jpg/500px-Hielos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ice cubes in a tray","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHielos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG/500px-Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG/1280px-Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG/500px-Ice_cubes_for_beverages_-_hollow_cylinders.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt